{% doc %}
  Below product media — PRIVATE container block, whitelisted only in `blocks/_product-details.liquid`.

  Marks a POSITION, not a layout. Its only job is to carry
  `data-show-below-product-media="true"`, so `product-information-below-media.js` relocates it —
  and everything inside it — into the media-column slot (`.product-information__below-gallery`,
  `sections/product-information.liquid`) at `min-width: 768px`, restoring it below that. This
  replaces the per-block `show_below_product_media` toggle: whitelisted children need no setting
  of their own.

  It has NO settings and NO box: the `.contents` helper (`src/scss/global/_helpers.scss`) makes the
  children direct children of whichever parent the container currently lives in — flex items of
  `.group-block-content` on mobile (so they inherit the Product-details row gap) and children of
  the slot on desktop (so spacing comes from each block's own `spacing-style`). Giving the
  container its own gap/padding settings would only duplicate what the real parent already
  provides.

  It stays a CHILD of `_product-details` (rather than a static block in the media column) because
  the relocation JS remembers the container's original sibling and restores it there on mobile —
  so the merchant's mobile ordering inside the Product details list is preserved. As a consequence
  the container moves as ONE node: on mobile all its children sit together at the container's
  position. For two different mobile positions, add two containers; on desktop they stack in DOM
  order inside the media column.

  Only move-safe blocks may be whitelisted here — a fork adding its own types to the `blocks` array
  must audit them first. `appendChild` MOVES a node, which fires `disconnectedCallback` then
  `connectedCallback` on every custom element inside: a component that creates its
  `AbortController` once per instance (rather than per connect) rebinds against an already-aborted
  signal and dies silently, with no console error. See `src/js/modules/video-card.js` for the safe
  idiom. `@theme` / `@app` are deliberately NOT accepted — the list is closed so every type in it
  has been checked.

  @example
  {% content_for 'block', type: '_product-below-media', id: 'below-media' %}
{% enddoc %}

{% capture children %}
  {% content_for 'blocks' %}
{% endcapture %}
{% assign children = children | strip %}

{%- comment -%}
  An empty container is still a child NODE of the slot, so `:empty` would stop matching there and
  `section-product-information.scss` would add `4rem` of margin around nothing. Keep it rendered in
  the editor so the block stays mapped while the merchant fills it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if children != blank or request.design_mode -%}
  <div
    class="product-below-media contents"
    data-show-below-product-media="true"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {{ children }}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

